{title: When I Think of Jesus}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
This is another collaboration with Lena, who has also written with my friend
Elton Smith at Songs of Praise. Lena sent me the music, and I
added the lyrics. Once again, I like the reflective nature of the music that Lena has composed.

Verse 2
When I Think of Jesus
Music by Lena Kittrell
Words by Larry Holder
Copyright © 2004 Lena Kittrell and Larry Holder

Verse 3
(verse 1)
When I think of al lthe ways He has blessed me
There is no doubt the Lord is my Friend.
I rest upon His promise:
This grace I've known shall never end.

Verse 4
Thinking back, now, to the day that He saved me
There is joy I cannot explain.
His grace and mercy found me
And by His grace, I'm born again.

Verse 5
Now Jesus guides me through the darkness
And He guides me through the day.
I'll never fear I've been forsaken
For Jesus is with me each step I take.

Verse 6
(verse 2)
When I think of all the joys of the journey
More precious now than silver or gold
I'm glad that I have chosen
The Way of Life, as time unfolds.

Verse 7
Then one day, the Lord will call me to heaven
There to be forever with Him.
All tears and pain forgotten;
His perfect peace will never end.

Verse 8
The stars above declare His glory
Far beyond what words express
And I am here to tell His story
Of mercy, deliv'rance, and holiness.

Verse 9
(Ending)
When I think of all the ways He has blessed me
There is no doubt the Lord is my Friend.
I rest upon His promise:
This grace I've known shall never end...
